        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">What do young adults most often bring?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">Between 18 and 29 the questions tend to come from the same places: direction, separation and comparison. Uncertainty in this period is not a shortcoming; it is a feature of the stage. These are the subjects we talk about most.</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-ink-muted">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Uncertainty about career or course, the sense of being on the wrong path</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Separating from family and difficulty setting boundaries</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Attachment and repeating patterns in relationships</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Comparison with peers and inadequacy fed by social media</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0 mt-2.5"></span>Uncertainty after graduation and the <a href="/en/blog/what-is-anxiety-disorder.html" class="text-primary underline hover:no-underline">anxiety</a> that comes with it</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
